cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NumSDE in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NumSDE: numerical methods for stochastic differential equations"
abstract: >-
  NumSDE is a Python library of numerical methods for stochastic differential
  equations, written for university teaching and research. It provides tested
  reference implementations of numerical schemes and tools for empirical
  convergence studies.
authors:
  - family-names: Kruse
    given-names: Raphael
    email: raphael.kruse@mathematik.uni-halle.de
    affiliation: Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8341-5097"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mlu-numerics/numsde"
url: "https://numsde.readthedocs.io"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - stochastic differential equations
  - numerical analysis
  - Euler-Maruyama
  - Milstein
  - Monte Carlo
